module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Away.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Smooth.Localization
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Smooth.SmoothAt
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Smoothing.CommonDesingularization
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Smoothing.LiftingLemma

/-!
# Lifting a desingularization

Let `R` be a Noetherian ring, let `Λ` be an `R`-algebra and let `π ∈ R` be an element whose
annihilator agrees with that of `π²` both in `R` and in `Λ`. Let `A` be an `R`-algebra of finite
presentation together with an `R`-algebra map `A → Λ` in which the image of `π` is strictly
standard over `R`. Given a factorization `A/π⁸A → C̄ → Λ/π⁸Λ` of the induced map with `C̄` of
finite presentation over `R/π⁸R`, the map `A → Λ` factors as `A → B → Λ` with `B` of finite
presentation over `R` such that `R_π → B_π` is smooth and such that

`H_{C̄/(R/π⁸R)} · Λ/π⁸Λ ⊆ √(H_{B/R}Λ) mod π⁸Λ`.

The lifting lemma, applied to the element `π⁴` and to `C̄` viewed as an algebra over
`R/(π⁴)²R = R/π⁸R`, produces `R → D → Λ` and a factorization `C̄ → D/π⁴D → Λ/π⁴Λ` with `R → D`
smooth at every prime not containing `π` and at every prime containing `π` which lies over a
prime of `C̄` at which `R/π⁸R → C̄` is smooth. The composite `A/π⁴A → C̄ → D/π⁴D` is a map
compatible with the maps to `Λ/π⁴Λ`, so the common desingularization of `A` and `D` applies and
yields `B` of finite presentation with factorizations `A → B → Λ` and `D → B → Λ` satisfying
`H_{D/R}B ⊆ H_{B/R}`.

Both conclusions follow from that inclusion. The image of `π` lies in `H_{D/R}`, since `R → D`
is smooth away from `π`; hence the image of `π` lies in `H_{B/R}` and `R → B` is smooth at every
prime not containing it. For `h ∈ H_{C̄/(R/π⁸R)}`, a preimage `z ∈ D` of the image of `h` in
`D/π⁴D` lies in `H_{D/R}`: a prime of `D` not containing `z` necessarily contains `π`, hence
contracts to a prime of `C̄` not containing `h`, at which `R/π⁸R → C̄` is smooth. So `z` maps
into `H_{B/R}Λ`, while the image of `h` in `Λ/π⁸Λ` differs from the image of `z` by a multiple
of `π⁴`, which lies in `H_{B/R}Λ` as well.

## Main definitions

There are no new definitions.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Smoothing.exists_finitePresentation_factorization_smoothAway_singularIdeal_le`: the
  factorization `A → B → Λ`, its smoothness after inverting `π`, and the inclusion of singular
  ideals modulo `π⁸`.

## Implementation notes

The factorization modulo `π⁸` is given by a ring map `A/π⁸A → C̄` together with the equations
saying that it is a map of `R/π⁸R`-algebras, and an `R/π⁸R`-algebra map `C̄ → Λ/π⁸Λ`; the
composite is required to be the reduction of `A → Λ`. The smoothness of `R_π → B_π` is stated
for the canonical `R_π`-algebra structure on `B_π` coming from `Localization.awayMap`.

